From: Eugene Bykov <omedius@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:49:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: advertise VHT beamformee STS 2 on MT7990

The MT7990 advertises VHT Beamformee STS Capability 3 (four space-time
streams) like the other mt7996 chips, but it only has two spatial streams
on 5 GHz. As a client of a 4x4 VHT AP at 160 MHz (AVM FRITZ!Box 7530), the
downlink collapses as soon as the AP starts explicit beamforming towards
it: UDP loss grows within seconds, TCP stalls for seconds at a time, and
retransmits reach the thousands. The link recovers when idle and breaks
again within a burst. A different station next to it stayed steady.

Clearing SU beamformee from the association request makes the link stable,
and advertising two space-time streams keeps beamforming usable. Measured
with a GL.iNet GL-MT3600BE (MT7990) as a station at 160 MHz, iperf3 against
a wired host through the AP, otherwise identical firmware and driver:

                      TCP down          TCP retransmits
  STS 4 (before)      6 - 92 Mbit/s     500 - 2000 per run
  STS 2 (after)       782 - 839 Mbit/s  0

UDP at 600 Mbit/s offered load lost up to 70% before and 0.2% (at 800
Mbit/s offered) after.

Use the value for two streams on MT7990 and leave MT7992 and MT7996
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Eugene Bykov <omedius@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/pull/1153
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/init.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/init.c
+++ b/mt7996/init.c
@@ -1351,6 +1351,8 @@ void mt7996_set_stream_vht_txbf_caps(str
 
 	if (is_mt7992(phy->mt76->dev))
 		*cap |= FIELD_PREP(IEEE80211_VHT_CAP_BEAMFORMEE_STS_MASK, 4);
+	else if (is_mt7990(phy->mt76->dev))
+		*cap |= FIELD_PREP(IEEE80211_VHT_CAP_BEAMFORMEE_STS_MASK, 1);
 	else
 		*cap |= FIELD_PREP(IEEE80211_VHT_CAP_BEAMFORMEE_STS_MASK, 3);
 
